    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2UhN1xQTPrFt9LAV1iuJfnY)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on `main` (includes #444); no stacking.\n- Independent of #444 in code: #444 only edits `aerospace.toml`/`aerospace.org`, this PR only edits `devonthink-open/`.\n- Merged in either order nothing breaks. If #444 were reverted, PDF windows would float again, but they would still be the only window raised.\n\n## What\n\n- Opening a PDF with DT Open ended with `activate`, which brings every DEVONthink window forward, including the main (database) window.\n- Now `open window for record` is followed by a System Events `AXRaise` of only that window.\n- New setting `DT_OPEN_RAISE` in `~/.config/dt-open/config`:\n  - `window` (default): raise only the PDF window.\n  - `app`: plain `activate` (old behaviour).\n  - `none`: never activate.\n- If raising fails (e.g. no Accessibility permission), the error goes to the log and the app falls back to `activate`.\n- `README.org` (literate source) and the tangled `open-handler.applescript` and `config` are updated together. Emacs was not available in the container, so the tangled files were edited by hand to match.\n\n## Not verified\n\n- Written in a Linux container: nothing was run, and the AppleScript was not compiled.\n- Not known whether `set frontmost` from System Events also pulls the main window forward; this is the main thing to test. If it does, try `DT_OPEN_RAISE=none` and tell me.\n- If DEVONthink is closed, it opens its own main window when it starts; this PR cannot prevent that.\n- AeroSpace (#444) may move focus to the workspace of whichever DEVONthink window is raised; check this when the main window sits on another workspace.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] Run `emacs --batch --eval \"(require 'org)\" --eval '(org-babel-tangle-file \"README.org\")'` in `devonthink-open/` and confirm `git diff` shows no change; then run `dt-open-install` (the script must compile).\n- [ ] Grant Accessibility permission to `DT Open PDF` (System Settings > Privacy & Security > Accessibility).\n- [ ] DEVONthink running with the main window open on another workspace/behind other apps: open an indexed PDF from Finder. Only the PDF window appears; the main window is not raised.\n- [ ] Same with the main window closed: only the PDF window appears, no main window.\n- [ ] Select two indexed PDFs in Finder, Cmd-O: both windows open, main window stays where it was.\n- [ ] Open a PDF that is not in DEVONthink: still opens in the fallback viewer.\n- [ ] Remove Accessibility permission: PDF still opens (falls back to `activate`), and `DT Open PDF.log` (with `DT_OPEN_DEBUG=1`) shows \"raising only the PDF window failed\".\n- [ ] `DT_OPEN_RAISE=app`: old behaviour (main window comes forward). `DT_OPEN_RAISE=none`: no raise.\n- [ ] With AeroSpace: the PDF window is tiled and focus goes to it (check #444 rule still applies).\n- [ ] DEVONthink closed, `DT_OPEN_LAUNCH=1`: PDF opens after launch; note whether the main window also appears.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9gHxz7b2vbwem1ECB)_",
